# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b2), edited. finneas_trout's first conversation.

~ start
set finneas_trout_met
Narrator: Ink, damp paper, and tallow smoke cling to the young man's cuffs as he adjusts his spectacles. He peers at you with the bright, restless posture of a city lecturer.
finneas_trout [smile]: Good evening! Strangers from beyond the mist, unless I miss my guess, and wide awake besides. I am Finneas Trout of Baskerton, presently instructing this village in basic reason.
* Ask for a lesson on the realm's lore -> shop_open
* Ask how a Baskerton scholar fares in Wickermoor -> about_self
* Ask about his studies of the Grey -> about_village
* Ask after the strange double he saw -> rumour
* [Insight DC 12] Notice the fine scented candles stacked on his desk -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ menu
finneas_trout [neutral]: Do ask if a question occurs to you. Inquiry is our best lantern against local superstition.
* Ask for a lesson on the realm's lore -> shop_open
* Ask how a Baskerton scholar fares in Wickermoor -> about_self
* Ask about his studies of the Grey -> about_village
* Ask after the strange double he saw -> rumour
* [Insight DC 12] Notice the fine scented candles stacked on his desk -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
finneas_trout [smile]: Gladly! Let us begin with the geography of Druskenvald and the six bells of the night.
-> menu

~ about_self
finneas_trout [weary]: I lodge at the inn and spend my hours persuading children that thunder is weather, not an angry spirit. Mayor Somerton means well, though his fondness for old customs tries my patience.
-> menu

~ about_village
finneas_trout [neutral]: I have been charting a malady called the Grey, where folk lose colour and heart until they fade into stupor. Superstition blames curses, yet every affliction has a mechanism.
-> menu

~ rumour
finneas_trout [afraid]: Odd that you are here, because I could swear I saw the spitting image of one of your party walk past the inn before the recent murders began. The likeness was uncanny.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: Half a dozen beeswax tapers sit wrapped in neat twine beside his inkwell, far more than one small room requires.
finneas_trout [smile]: Oh, those are from Oswick Frey's chandlery, as I happen to read late and require reliable light. Mr. Frey is a remarkably thoughtful conversationalist for such a rustic parish.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
finneas_trout [neutral]: A scholar goes through a dreadful number of candles in a realm without a sunrise, I assure you.
-> menu
